{
  "dom_id": "step-q92567",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Given that $(x,y)=(3,2)$ is a solution of the Diophantine equation $8x-5y=14,$ which of the following gives the general solution to the equation? \n\n*Hint: Assume that $t=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…\\,.$*",
  "worked_solution": "First, recall that a linear Diophantine equation\n\n$$\nax+by=c\n$$\n\nhas a solution if and only if $d\\,|\\,c,$ where $d=\\text{gcd}(a,b).$ Moreover, if $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ is a solution to the equation, then the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n({x}_{0}+\\frac{b}{d}t,\\,{y}_{0}-\\frac{a}{d}t),\\,t=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…\n$$\n\nHere, we have $a=8,$ $b=-5,$ $c=14,$ and\n\n$$\nd=\\text{gcd}(8,-5)=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $(3,2)$ is a solution of $8x-5y=14,$ the general solution must be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+\\frac{(-5)}{1}t,\\,2-\\frac{8}{1}t) & =(3-5t,\\,2-8t),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…\\,.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
